Port patch 0003 - tell the host scheduler when a thread is destroyed
Why: each N64 thread runs on a host thread (src/ultra/os_sched.c). When osDestroyThread removes a thread, its host thread must stop
being a scheduling target; the hook is called after the thread is off every queue and before the next thread is chosen.

--- a/lib/ultralib/src/os/destroythread.c
+++ b/lib/ultralib/src/os/destroythread.c
@@ -1,5 sha256=51f74afc3b8ae6cccb0ea0f80f7551e4aa9b8c0c6fcaf868c1d3d23feac77811 @@
=2
+
+/* PORT: tells the host scheduler layer (src/ultra/os_sched.c) that this thread's host thread is finished. */
+extern void __osHostThreadDestroyed(OSThread* t);
=3
@@ -41,6 sha256=73017e59478e1fabdc9519dac0d6d22df3461d2bd145a044c6412bfe52f0a70d @@
=3
+    __osHostThreadDestroyed(t); /* PORT */
+
=3
